Four actionable gaps remain in the prerequisite:

- **Freeze complete automask definitions before implementation.** The plan specifies defaults but omits hard/soft ranges and the concrete unit token (`ROTATION`, not `RADIANS`). `Definition.validate()` checks both input and rounded FLOAT32 against bounds; a maximum of mathematical `pi/2` would reject its rounded default. Specify canonical bounds and exact default tests against [brush.h:119](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/engine/source/brush/brush.h:119). See [registry.py:180](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/registry.py:180).

- **Explicitly separate static from unavailable-stack handling.** Generic static definitions currently report `stack=True`; native SIZE aliases report `stack=False`. Calling `prepare_stack()` uniformly therefore rejects valid alias snapshots. Branch only for unavailable **static** stacks, preserve `stack_available=False` and execution diagnostics, and test that unavailable **dynamic** stacks still reject. See [storage.py:166](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/storage.py:166), [commands.py:52](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/commands.py:52).

- **Define how dormant SIZE fields are validated.** `size_block()` merely copies fields; `value_domain(SIZE)` describes only the active representation. Reusing that domain for both fields would reject valid world sizes or accept invalid dormant data. Require separate pixel/world native domains, strict primitive types and mode validation, plus agreement between the active field and resolved value. Add malformed dormant-field cases for both owners. See [adapters.py:113](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/adapters.py:113) and [adapters.py:150](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/adapters.py:150).

- **Make registration regression expectations explicit.** Add a separate engine-definition catalogue to the initial registration union; do not broaden the legacy `DEFINITIONS` alias used by manifest diagnostics. Expected production counts become **27 definitions, still 62 curve declarations**. Test repeated registration and DLL-off reads of all four new defaults; current DLL-off assertions exercise legacy fields. See [authoring.py:14](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/authoring.py:14), [curves.py:51](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/sculptcore_addon/brush_properties/curves.py:51), [test_frozen_authoring.py:121](/C:/dev/blender/sculptcore-blender-addon/claudeMemory/scripts/test_frozen_authoring.py:121).

The separate engine-owned IDs and proposed defaults agree with the frozen contract. No edits, builds, tests or delegation performed.
